    "rationale": "TaiCOL and Tai2 provide no exact species record. Kew POWO explicitly treats the book name Laburnum vulgare as a synonym of Laburnum anagyroides. A Taiwan government standards document independently uses Laburnum anagyroides (= Cytisus laburnum L.), while a Taiwan public horticultural source explicitly pairs 金鏈花 (歐洲金鏈花) with Laburnum anagyroides. Because no Taiwan government or academic Chinese species name was found, 金鏈花 is marked as a lower-priority Taiwan-public fallback; no Taiwan occurrence is asserted."
